{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>I am El Shaddai.</b> By My name I swear, as in וְאָמַרְתִּי חַי אָנֹכִי לְעוֹלָם (Deuteronomy 32:40). And in this form alone do we find an oath by the blessed El to Jacob." "<b>Be fruitful and multiply.</b> And do not fear that your seed will be destroyed by the hand of the nations, even when the seed is unfit. Therefore do not cease from being fruitful and multiplying — the opposite of the counsel of Rabbi Ishmael, who said: From the day the wicked kingdom spread, it is a decree upon us not to marry and beget children, and so the seed of Abraham our father would perish from the world. But this is because I, being El Shaddai, have no need for a prepared recipient; I will fulfill what I have said in any case, even without a prepared recipient." "<b>And kings shall come from your loins.</b> Men fit for kingship, so that you will not need to place a foreigner over yourself — as in the case of the kings of Edom (Genesis 36:31–39): Samlah of Masrekah, Saul of Rehoboth-by-the-River, and others."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {1 "The Talmudic quote (b. Bava Batra 60b) is rendered as Sforno cites it; the bracketed [אָבִינוּ] 'our father' is included as it appears in the source text."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:25.058422376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}